    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "ctB3K",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -1282,
      "name": "Model Card",
      "context": "Shared model card using the user-supplied catalog. Three lines: the name (with the Active badge), the short purpose with its icon on its own line, then the tags row: languages, optional native-streaming support, CPU fit, and practical package size. Same arrangement in Local and Browse. CPU fit comes from the catalog cpuFit: excellent = Great on CPU (success icon), good = Good on CPU (neutral icon, the default), heavy = Heavy on CPU (warning icon); the label always states the level so color is never the only cue. Package sizes can differ by platform/runtime; streaming badges must reflect the shipped backend. Active uses accent border and badge, and on Local it is always the first card; a downloaded Browse card is subdued, except that a card with a runtime selector keeps its content undimmed so the selector stays usable. Cards of models with several runtimes show the runtime selector on Browse too. Download progress is a design example at 38%. The tags row wraps in the app when the window is narrow; the order is kept.",
