                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "j3xOUJ",
                  "x": 60,
                  "y": 0,
                  "name": "Model Runtime Select",
                  "context": "Runtime selector on a model card, placed before the primary action (Use model on Local, Download on Browse), so the runtime is chosen and then used. No visible Runtime label; accessible name: Runtime for [model]. Automatic displays Auto (resolved runtime); a manual selection displays only the runtime name. On Local the choices are Automatic and the runtimes whose files are downloaded; on Browse they are Automatic and every runtime this build can run for the model, and the card's size, Streaming badge and Download state follow the selection (each runtime's files are downloaded and kept separately). Models with a single runtime show no selector. Language model cards have none: they have one runtime, and the hardware choice is parked. The app widens the field so Auto (transcribe.cpp) fits.",
