    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "jm5Yg",
      "x": 918,
      "y": -388,
      "name": "Model Runtime Select Menu",
      "context": "Open menu below a card's runtime selector, which sits before Use model (Local) or Download (Browse). Options: Automatic, then the runtimes available for that model, so the list differs per model (the example is Nemotron 3.5: sherpa-onnx, parakeet.cpp and transcribe.cpp). Each option shows its state at the right: Downloaded (check mark) for a runtime whose files are on this computer, otherwise the size of the download; the selection is the accent row with a check, and Automatic names the runtime it resolves to. Browse lists every runtime this build can run; Local lists only the downloaded ones, which all show Downloaded. The closed selector shows Auto (resolved runtime) or the runtime name only. Each model has an independent selection. Screen readers hear the state with the name, for example \"sherpa-onnx, downloaded\". In the app the state is part of each option's text on Browse (\"sherpa-onnx · Downloaded\", \"parakeet.cpp · 984 MB\") and the closed selector shows the selected option's text; Local lists plain runtime names, since all of them are downloaded.",
