    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "NituI",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -1497,
      "name": "Recording Card",
      "context": "Shared recording session card. Transcript preview clamped to two lines, then one metadata row: time recorded and audio duration only (no language or model). When the dictation was post-processed, the transcript is the result of the last process in the chain, the text that was inserted, and a row (hidden by default) offers the original transcript, and when the last process was a decision model an Action Result replaces the text and shows which action ran. The processes are not named, since there can be several. A recording without a transcript (no model was chosen, or transcription failed) shows a muted note instead of text, and a failed one also shows the error. Actions: Copy transcript (copies the final text; shows ‘Copied’ for 2 seconds; disabled without a transcript), Retranscribe (runs the stored audio again through the currently active speech model and then the same processes, skipping any that were deleted; the previous text is kept until the new one succeeds; disabled while running and when no usable model is active) and Delete (asks for confirmation, removes audio and transcript). Player row: play/pause, elapsed time, scrubbable progress slider, total duration. Only one card plays at a time. The slider geometry is fixed for the 960-pixel column.",
      "reusable": true,
      "width": 960,
      "fill": "$content-bg",
