    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "qWs7M",
      "x": 1000,
      "y": -1760,
      "name": "Shared Shortcut Notice",
      "context": "Shown under a shortcut when other things use the same shortcut: below Start dictation on Controls when post-processing processes use it (they are then the default post-processing and run after every dictation), and below the shortcut on a process's edit screen. On the dictation shortcut its title is Default post-processing; on another shared shortcut it reads Shared with N other processes. It lists what runs, in order, and links to Post Processing where the order is changed. It is information only, never an error: sharing a shortcut with dictation or with other processes is allowed (only the cancel shortcut must differ).",
      "reusable": true,
      "width": 960,
      "fill": "$accent-soft",
      "cornerRadius": 8,
