    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "WPT6d",
      "x": 2100,
      "y": -2480,
      "name": "Voice Command Row",
      "context": "One command of a command set on its edit screen. The name and the description are what the decision model reads to match what was said, so the description should read like the phrases a person would say. The right side shows the action (Press keys) and the key press. The pencil opens the row for editing in place (Voice Command Row · Editing); Delete removes the command without a dialog (Revert on the screen brings it back until Save). The order of commands does not matter to the model, so rows are sorted A–Z by name and have no grip. The keys show at most the first three presses, then a muted \"+n\" for the rest, so a long sequence never runs into the buttons; the full sequence is in the edit form.",
      "reusable": true,
      "width": 960,
